{"id":"rondonia","name":"Rondônia deforestation arc","country":"Brazil","story":"Dry-season (Jul–Oct) clearing fires along the Amazon arc of deforestation.","places":["Rondônia","Porto Velho","Ariquemes"],"lang":["pt"],"bbox":[-64.5,-11.8,-61.0,-8.5],"grid_deg":0.1,"data_through":"2026-11-10","built_at":"2026-11-10T16:40:20+00:00","estimand":{"primary":"Hotspots per period on the Aqua MODIS scale: the number of vegetation-fire detections Aqua MODIS would have recorded (early-afternoon and post-midnight passes). Day and night are calibrated separately and added.","why_aqua":"The early-afternoon orbit is the only one observed continuously from 2002 (Aqua) through Suomi-NPP, NOAA-20 and NOAA-21. Converting VIIRS to MODIS scale discards information and is well-posed; the reverse must invent small fires MODIS never saw, so the VIIRS-scale view is marked modelled before 2012.","secondary":["Fire cell-days (0.1° cell × UTC day with ≥1 detection), Aqua scale","Hotspots on the Suomi-NPP VIIRS scale (modelled before 2012)","Persistent heat sources (kilns, flares, industry, volcanoes) harmonized separately","Raw detections — not comparable across satellite eras"],"not":"Not burned area and not a count of fires: a detection is one hot pixel in one overpass."},"method":{"confidence_filter":"drop VIIRS 'l' and MODIS confidence < 30 (no crosswalk between the two scales); sensitivity reported","static_mask":"0.01° cells where science-quality FIRMS `type` is 1–3 for ≥50% of ≥3 detections","coverage":"share of days each satellite delivered data anywhere on Earth in each period (measured, so launches, gaps and the Suomi-NPP end come from the data); below 25% a satellite is left out, otherwise counts are divided by coverage","calibration":"ratio of totals per calendar month, day and night separately, shrunk toward the pooled ratio by empirical Bayes (shrinkage strength estimated from the data). Chain: Terra→Aqua (2002–2020, bridges 2000–2002 only), Suomi-NPP→Aqua (2012–2020, pre-drift), NOAA-20→Suomi-NPP, NOAA-21→NOAA-20; chain-closure mismatch is added to the error","combination":"inverse-variance mean of the satellites observing each period (calibration error + counting noise, evaluated at the pooled mean); intervals widened so 95% of held-out months fall inside (MODIS-denial test)","comparison":"each period vs the same month/week in other complete years: median, ratio, percentile, rank — no sigma thresholds (fire counts are skewed)","weekly":"ISO-8601 weeks; weeks use their Thursday's month calibration","provisional":"periods containing near-real-time rows are provisional: FIRMS replaces NRT with standard processing after ~3 months, and the mirror keeps only one of the two, so the NRT-to-standard difference cannot be measured from it"},"calibration":{"veg_det_D":[{"sensor":"MODIS_T","reference":"MODIS_A","window":["2002-08","2020-12"],"beta":[5.2013,3.9352,4.6761,2.7718,3.5936,3.0739,2.8649,2.6117,3.4184,4.5387,4.8051,6.5847],"pooled":3.2442,"sigma2":0.4012,"tau2":0.1244,"n_periods":218,"calibrated":true},{"sensor":"VIIRS_SNPP","reference":"MODIS_A","window":["2012-02","2020-12"],"beta":[0.1816,0.2193,0.3209,0.2104,0.1826,0.2331,0.27,0.2462,0.2454,0.1979,0.1918,0.2646],"pooled":0.2371,"sigma2":0.066,"tau2":0.0408,"n_periods":107,"calibrated":true},{"sensor":"VIIRS_NOAA20","reference":"VIIRS_SNPP","window":["2018-05","2026-10"],"beta":[1.0215,1.0232,1.0227,1.0226,1.0119,1.0325,1.0268,1.0276,1.0139,1.0086,1.0536,1.0139],"pooled":1.0218,"sigma2":0.0378,"tau2":0.0002,"n_periods":97,"calibrated":true},{"sensor":"VIIRS_NOAA21","reference":"VIIRS_NOAA20","window":["2024-02","2026-10"],"beta":[0.7537,0.7718,1.3198,0.9512,1.1708,0.9499,1.1021,1.0922,0.9907,1.2295,1.3211,0.6731],"pooled":1.0801,"sigma2":0.0025,"tau2":0.0916,"n_periods":31,"calibrated":true}],"veg_det_N":[{"sensor":"MODIS_T","reference":"MODIS_A","window":["2002-08","2020-12"],"beta":[0.3841,0.441,0.5378,0.5213,0.4853,0.4105,0.4177,0.4724,0.4473,0.3877,0.318,0.4812],"pooled":0.4514,"sigm